  "notes": "USAGE:\nAs a する verb, {移行|いこう}する means \"to transition to\" or \"to migrate to.\" The particle に marks the destination: ～に{移行|いこう}する. Often used for planned, organized transitions rather than spontaneous changes.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {移行|いこう}{期間|きかん}: transition period\n- {移行|いこう}{作業|さぎょう}: migration work\n- ～に{移行|いこう}する: to transition to ~\n- {段階的|だんかいてき}に{移行|いこう}する: to transition in stages\n- スムーズに{移行|いこう}する: to transition smoothly\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{変更|へんこう} means \"change\" or \"modification\" and focuses on altering something specific. {移行|いこう} implies a broader shift from one state or system to another and typically involves a process over time.",
